{
  "title": "Taweez against Knee Pains",
  "data": "Recite the first seven verses of [Surah al-Fath](A52).\nAfter the ritual prayers, recite:\nيَا اَجْوَدَ مَنْ اَعْطٰى يَا خَيْرَ مَنْ سُئِلَ وَيَاۤ اَرْحَمَ مَنِ اسْتُرْحِمَ اِرْحَمْ ضَعْفِىْ وَقِلَّةَ حِيْلَتِىْ وَاَعْفِنِىْ مِنْ وَجَعِىْ\nYAA AJWADA MAN A'TAA YAA KHAYRA MAN SU-IL WA YAA ARHAMA MANIS TURHIM, IRHAM DA'FEE WA QILLATA HEELATEE WA A'FINEE MIN WAJA-I'\nO most Generous of all who give, O best of all who are asked, O most Merciful of all who are besought for mercy: have mercy on my weakness and my scant resourcefulness, and relieve me of my pain.\nRecite this verse 7 times over the legs:\nوَاتْلُ مَاۤ اُوْحِىَ اِلَيْكَ مِنْ كِتَابِ رَبِّكَ لَا مُبَدِّلَ لِكَلِمَاتِهٖ وَلَنْ تَجِدَ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖ مُلْتَحَدًا\nWATLU MAA OOHIYA ILAYKA MIN KITAABI RABBIKA LAA MUBADDILA LI-KALIMAATIHI WA LAN TAJIDA MIN DOONIHI MULTAHADAA\nAnd recite what has been revealed to you of the Book of your Lord; there is none who can change His words, and you will not find besides Him any refuge.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Fath: Quoted from the book Tibb al-A'immah (Medicine of the Imams), Jabir al-Ju'fi reported Imam Muhammad al-Baqir (a) as saying: I was present with al-Husayn ibn Ali (a) when a man from the descendants of Umayyah, yet loyal to us, came to him and said, \"O son of Allah's Messenger, I could hardly come to you walking, because of a pain from which I am suffering in my leg.\" The Imam (a) asked, \"How is it you have turned away from the supplicatory amulet of al-Hasan ibn Ali (a)?\" \"What is that, son of Allah's Messenger?\" asked the man. The Imam (a) explained, \"Recite the first seven verses of [Surah al-Fath](A52).\" Afterwards, the man said, \"As I had carried out this direction, I felt no pain at all.\"\n\nDua after the prayers: It is also reported that one who suffers from knee pains may say this supplicatory prayer after the ritual prayers:\n\nVerse over the legs: For those suffering from pains in the legs, it is reportedly recommended to recite this holy verse seven times over the legs:"
}
